WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.794 --> 00:00:13.317
Previously on Dead City.

2
00:00:14.144 --> 00:00:16.320
Titicaca wants to know when
the sweet jams can return.

3
00:00:16.494 --> 00:00:18.854
Stop pretending like you can
talk to those toothless freaks.

4
00:00:18.931 --> 00:00:20.411
Luis said he's gonna quiz me on this.

5
00:00:20.498 --> 00:00:21.673
I don't think I'm ready yet.

6
00:00:21.804 --> 00:00:23.893
You are. One breath. one motion.

7
00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:25.764
We could plow
Central Park. grow more food.

8
00:00:25.938 --> 00:00:27.114
bring in even more people.

9
00:00:27.288 --> 00:00:29.725
You don't want just more people.

10
00:00:30.813 --> 00:00:32.380
You want good people.

11
00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:34.338
And I hate to be the one
to break it to you.

12
00:00:34.512 --> 00:00:35.750
I don't know that there's a lot of

13
00:00:35.774 --> 00:00:36.774
good people left.

14
00:00:37.994 --> 00:00:39.300
I guess we'll find out.

15
00:01:02.888 --> 00:01:04.281
Hey.

16
00:01:04.367 --> 00:01:05.543
Need that?

17
00:01:06.718 --> 00:01:07.718
Thanks.

18
00:01:09.634 --> 00:01:11.071
Is Negan around?

19
00:01:11.158 --> 00:01:12.376
Yeah. big man's upstairs.

20
00:01:13.029 --> 00:01:14.900
Is that from a deadie
you dropped outside?

21
00:01:14.987 --> 00:01:17.425
'Cause I could use a few for my CLVFC.

22
00:01:17.902 --> 00:01:19.340
Negan mentioned your food chain.

23
00:01:20.123 --> 00:01:21.298
Yeah.

24
00:01:21.646 --> 00:01:24.736
See. you got the maggots.
and they just eat up the rot.

25
00:01:25.085 --> 00:01:27.304
They just strip it all down to nothin'.

26
00:01:28.088 --> 00:01:30.133
And then out of that nothin' comes...

27
00:01:30.264 --> 00:01:31.526
somethin' good.

28
00:01:32.265 --> 00:01:34.094
And that's somethin' that can sustain life.

29
00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.795
You know. nothin' wasted.
not even the deadies.

30
00:01:40.578 --> 00:01:42.145
My dad used to say the same thing.

31
00:01:42.276 --> 00:01:43.276
about farming.

32
00:01:44.408 --> 00:01:45.496
Yeah?

33
00:01:45.583 --> 00:01:46.646
Everything that you put into the soil

34
00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:48.020
comes back to you.

35
00:01:48.151 --> 00:01:50.191
Sounds like Papa Magpie
had his finger on the pulse.

36
00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:53.983
Dirt don't lie.

37
00:01:54.505 --> 00:01:59.467
Now whether it comes from
seed or bone...

38
00:02:00.642 --> 00:02:01.904
Yesterday's somebody.

39
00:02:02.731 --> 00:02:04.820
If you treat it right.

40
00:02:04.907 --> 00:02:06.822
man. it is gonna pay you back
every time.

41
00:02:09.824 --> 00:02:11.000
It's one of the last promises

42
00:02:11.087 --> 00:02:12.915
left in this world. as far as I'm concerned.

43
00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:17.659
Well. that and how shoelaces
always wear out

44
00:02:17.746 --> 00:02:19.878
before the boot. What is up with that?

45
00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:23.839
- Negan's upstairs?
- Yes ma'am.

46
00:02:26.624 --> 00:02:28.224
No. no. no. no. no. Hey. buddy. come on.

47
00:02:28.278 --> 00:02:30.106
Rein it in. Hey. cut that shit out.

48
00:02:30.193 --> 00:02:31.499
You are gonna screw up your arm

49
00:02:31.629 --> 00:02:32.674
all over again.

50
00:02:32.761 --> 00:02:34.502
You gotta stop! Maggie?

51
00:02:34.589 --> 00:02:35.938
Can you toss me that duct tape

52
00:02:36.025 --> 00:02:37.548
at the end of the bar please?

53
00:02:38.245 --> 00:02:40.029
Cockenspiel. stop. What are you doing?

54
00:02:40.464 --> 00:02:42.204
Would you please hold it in?

55
00:02:42.466 --> 00:02:44.773
Hey. is "pretty" worth losing
an arm over. kid?

56
00:02:45.861 --> 00:02:48.341
Negan. can you hold him down
while I duct tape him?

57
00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:50.474
No.

58
00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:54.826
So are you here to tell me
about your big night?

59
00:02:55.349 --> 00:02:57.525
I saw your little light show.

60
00:02:57.612 --> 00:03:00.528
Well. I figured we should
put up a welcome sign.

61
00:03:02.007 --> 00:03:03.531
Did you hear about the other thing?

62
00:03:06.186 --> 00:03:07.839
The Dama killed herself.

63
00:03:10.538 --> 00:03:12.888
Alright. well.
I guess she made her choice.

64
00:03:14.629 --> 00:03:15.978
I thought I'd feel...

65
00:03:19.982 --> 00:03:21.679
I don't know what I thought I'd feel.

66
00:03:21.766 --> 00:03:23.638
Well. I don't know.

67
00:03:23.725 --> 00:03:27.207
I think that you should feel good.

68
00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:29.861
The old hag. she did you a favor.

69
00:03:31.733 --> 00:03:33.996
Alright. is there anything else
from the daily debrief

70
00:03:34.126 --> 00:03:36.085
that will be of interest to me?

71
00:03:36.738 --> 00:03:38.218
Season is turning.

72
00:03:39.393 --> 00:03:41.873
Everybody is clearing Central Park.

73
00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:43.571
We got to plant before the frost.

74
00:03:44.746 --> 00:03:46.487
And we can certainly use your help.

75
00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:50.012
That's a good one.

76
00:03:51.970 --> 00:03:53.929
You're being serious.

77
00:03:55.800 --> 00:03:59.413
I can't. I got some shit
to tend to in my own house.

78
00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:24.394
Alright. look.

79
00:04:26.004 --> 00:04:27.615
I am done with you playing patty-cake

80
00:04:27.745 --> 00:04:30.487
with two flesh sacks in your bar all day.

81
00:04:30.574 --> 00:04:32.924
So you killing Scraps here?

82
00:04:33.011 --> 00:04:36.101
It's the first step in you
becoming a half civilized

83
00:04:36.232 --> 00:04:38.756
human male who can still get laid

84
00:04:38.843 --> 00:04:40.683
before the moths finish eating
that sock puppet

85
00:04:40.758 --> 00:04:42.107
you call a dick.

86
00:04:42.194 --> 00:04:44.632
Your dick's a freaking decorative spoon.

87
00:04:44.762 --> 00:04:46.547
Brother. do it.

88
00:04:50.725 --> 00:04:52.944
Okay.

89
00:05:03.607 --> 00:05:07.568
Help... me.

90
00:05:12.355 --> 00:05:14.314
She's not even a danger. brother.

91
00:05:16.011 --> 00:05:18.535
I need to know that I can trust you

92
00:05:18.666 --> 00:05:20.145
if shit hits the fan.

93
00:05:30.982 --> 00:05:32.854
Yeah. actually. fuck this. man. Fuck this.

94
00:05:33.376 --> 00:05:34.551
Actually. fuck you.

95
00:05:34.638 --> 00:05:36.466
'Cause I take out plenty of deadies

96
00:05:36.597 --> 00:05:37.815
for the chain. brother.

97
00:05:38.338 --> 00:05:40.557
The real question is. what is it to you

98
00:05:40.688 --> 00:05:41.969
if I got some I talk to sometimes?

99
00:05:41.993 --> 00:05:43.710
Alright. well the first thing
I'd say to that is

100
00:05:43.734 --> 00:05:44.909
they're not people.

101
00:05:44.996 --> 00:05:46.694
But wait a minute.
what about Cole Brewer

102
00:05:46.824 --> 00:05:49.044
or fucking Razer McNab?
Are those people?

103
00:05:49.174 --> 00:05:50.611
Let me answer that for you. Negan.

104
00:05:50.698 --> 00:05:52.787
No. they're god damn
video game characters.

105
00:05:52.917 --> 00:05:55.790
Okay? I was holed up all alone
for a fucking eternity.

106
00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:57.095
What is your excuse?

107
00:06:01.839 --> 00:06:03.145
Shit.

108
00:06:08.193 --> 00:06:09.934
That's Fabian's flare.

109
00:06:10.065 --> 00:06:11.521
He must have spotted something
on the river.

110
00:06:11.545 --> 00:06:12.894
Let's go.

111
00:06:24.384 --> 00:06:27.082
Whoa! I wasn't expecting
the Fuckyouville

112
00:06:27.169 --> 00:06:28.257
welcoming committee.

113
00:06:28.344 --> 00:06:30.346
Don't get it scrambled. neighbor.

114
00:06:30.433 --> 00:06:33.523
You gamble on people.
We protect our pile.

115
00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:36.308
Just so happens the shit you kick loose

116
00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:38.572
rolls downhill.

117
00:06:53.978 --> 00:06:55.778
We've got to get
these people to the hospital.

118
00:08:06.834 --> 00:08:08.531
You're gonna be okay. alright?

119
00:08:08.662 --> 00:08:09.880
Is anyone bit?

120
00:08:10.011 --> 00:08:13.797
No. This was people.
A crew out of Newark.

121
00:08:13.928 --> 00:08:15.669
Been raiding us for years.

122
00:08:15.756 --> 00:08:17.279
Taking everything they could.

123
00:08:17.409 --> 00:08:19.257
We saw the statue last night
and were packing up

124
00:08:19.281 --> 00:08:21.239
what little we had left to check it out.

125
00:08:21.326 --> 00:08:24.242
But they hit us at dawn and set
the whole damn place on fire.

126
00:08:24.373 --> 00:08:26.288
Belleville ain't nothin' but ashes now.

127
00:08:26.418 --> 00:08:27.768
So you followed the light?

128
00:08:30.422 --> 00:08:32.250
Suspected it might be a trap.

129
00:08:32.337 --> 00:08:34.337
Took a chance on the hope
it meant what it used to.

130
00:08:35.818 --> 00:08:37.038
Does it?

131
00:08:41.346 --> 00:08:42.957
It does.

132
00:08:43.044 --> 00:08:45.109
Give me your tired. your poor.
and your huddled masses. right?

133
00:08:45.133 --> 00:08:46.221
Okay. listen up. everyone.

134
00:08:46.351 --> 00:08:48.615
I need every able-bodied person

135
00:08:48.702 --> 00:08:50.201
to help bring the wounded to the hospital.

136
00:08:50.225 --> 00:08:52.183
Streets are a mess.
Cars are not getting through.

137
00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:55.926
so it is walk or be carried
all the way down Amsterdam.

138
00:08:56.318 --> 00:08:58.799
Hey. thank you for your help.

139
00:08:58.929 --> 00:09:01.671
I still think lighting
that statue was a bad idea.

140
00:09:01.758 --> 00:09:03.717
It doesn't mean I won't do my job.

141
00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.284
Hey. Bauer.

142
00:09:06.371 --> 00:09:08.243
These Newark assholes.

143
00:09:08.373 --> 00:09:09.853
are they the kind to come after you?

144
00:09:10.288 --> 00:09:13.465
Because if they're coming.
they're coming after all of us.

145
00:09:14.510 --> 00:09:16.643
We need
to get everyone somewhere safe.

146
00:09:16.730 --> 00:09:17.948
Injured to the hospital.

147
00:09:18.079 --> 00:09:19.535
the rest of these people
safe to an apartment.

148
00:09:19.559 --> 00:09:20.879
I'm gonna get word to the armory.

149
00:09:20.995 --> 00:09:21.995
get weapons and backup.

150
00:09:22.083 --> 00:09:23.321
After that. head to the hospital.

151
00:09:23.345 --> 00:09:24.757
You handle the home front.
I handle Newark.

152
00:09:24.781 --> 00:09:26.174
- Okay.
- Okay.

153
00:09:29.133 --> 00:09:30.439
Really?

154
00:09:30.526 --> 00:09:32.286
So you're just gonna play
Florence Nightingale

155
00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:34.486
when a boatload of bad people show up?

156
00:09:34.617 --> 00:09:36.663
Yeah. 'cause Renata knows
what she's doing.

157
00:09:36.793 --> 00:09:38.099
Does she?

158
00:09:38.186 --> 00:09:39.927
She kept her family alive for 15 years

159
00:09:40.057 --> 00:09:41.972
without killing anybody or using an army.

160
00:09:42.059 --> 00:09:43.670
Right. until The Croat showed up.

161
00:09:43.757 --> 00:09:45.759
And she lost two of hers.
How many have you lost?

162
00:09:45.889 --> 00:09:48.892
When she cracks. Maggie. and she will.

163
00:09:49.023 --> 00:09:51.634
then it's gonna be on you
to keep your son breathing.

164
00:09:51.721 --> 00:09:54.594
So the sooner you step up.
the safer we'll all be.

165
00:10:02.471 --> 00:10:04.560
Green is for non-life-threatening injuries.

166
00:10:04.691 --> 00:10:05.971
If they can walk. they're green.

167
00:10:06.083 --> 00:10:07.147
If they can talk. they're purple.

168
00:10:07.171 --> 00:10:08.390
And red? Red means

169
00:10:08.477 --> 00:10:10.827
handcuff your patient to their bed. okay?

170
00:10:10.958 --> 00:10:11.828
Let's go! Go.

171
00:10:11.915 --> 00:10:12.960
Come on.

172
00:10:15.789 --> 00:10:16.853
You've gotta be the youngest doctor

173
00:10:16.877 --> 00:10:18.139
I've ever seen.

174
00:10:18.269 --> 00:10:19.619
I'm just an apprentice. actually.

175
00:10:23.623 --> 00:10:25.407
I just grabbed it in the fire.

176
00:10:25.537 --> 00:10:26.930
I don't know why.

177
00:10:27.017 --> 00:10:28.323
You can't play with one domino.

178
00:10:28.889 --> 00:10:29.977
It's a game?

179
00:10:31.108 --> 00:10:32.109
Yeah.

180
00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:33.589
It's a family tradition.

181
00:10:34.198 --> 00:10:36.592
Out of all of them. I grabbed this one.

182
00:10:37.332 --> 00:10:39.160
It's bad luck. Big six.

183
00:10:39.508 --> 00:10:40.828
That's what my uncle always said.

184
00:10:40.857 --> 00:10:42.250
Well. you got here.

185
00:10:43.294 --> 00:10:44.934
Maybe your luck's starting
to turn around.

186
00:10:47.472 --> 00:10:48.580
Sure as hell didn't expect all this

187
00:10:48.604 --> 00:10:49.779
when we followed the light.

188
00:10:49.866 --> 00:10:52.216
It's a good place. And with a great doctor.

189
00:10:52.869 --> 00:10:56.003
And he'll set your arm
once things die down.

190
00:11:06.013 --> 00:11:09.625
Do not fucking fire
unless I fucking signal.

191
00:11:09.712 --> 00:11:12.846
- You got it?
- Whatever you say. boss lady.

192
00:11:18.808 --> 00:11:20.549
Put your weapons down. everyone.

193
00:11:20.636 --> 00:11:22.333
Weapons down.

194
00:11:22.812 --> 00:11:26.120
Luis! Stab wound from Newark.

195
00:11:26.207 --> 00:11:27.208
Take her to trauma one.

196
00:11:27.338 --> 00:11:29.253
Whoa! Hell no!

197
00:11:29.384 --> 00:11:31.865
You put us in here with them.
they're gonna kill us.

198
00:11:31.952 --> 00:11:33.649
Y- y-you're making a mistake.

199
00:11:33.736 --> 00:11:35.869
Newark attacked us.
and they'll attack you.

200
00:11:35.956 --> 00:11:37.871
And you've got too much to lose.

201
00:11:39.481 --> 00:11:41.135
Newark washed up even worse off.

202
00:11:41.222 --> 00:11:42.939
They're saying
that Belleville attacked them.

203
00:11:42.963 --> 00:11:46.009
Alright. so we've got
to treat enemies side by side.

204
00:11:46.096 --> 00:11:47.683
I think until we figure out
what's going on.

205
00:11:47.707 --> 00:11:49.336
the only thing to do is to help them all.

206
00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:51.040
I confiscated Belleville's
weapons already.

207
00:11:51.101 --> 00:11:52.537
And I took Newark's.

208
00:11:52.668 --> 00:11:54.864
We're gonna post up guards.
and we'll minimize the danger.

209
00:11:54.888 --> 00:11:58.282
We turned on that light.
They are here because of us.

210
00:11:58.413 --> 00:11:59.849
I have to figure out who can stay.

211
00:11:59.980 --> 00:12:01.958
But if our people get hurt
before I can do that. I-

212
00:12:01.982 --> 00:12:03.699
That is not gonna happen.
I'm not gonna let it happen.

213
00:12:03.723 --> 00:12:05.072
That's my job.

214
00:12:05.159 --> 00:12:07.119
Your job is to make
the best choice for all of us.

215
00:12:09.206 --> 00:12:10.599
More incoming.

216
00:12:20.304 --> 00:12:22.021
Can't we give her something more
for the pain?

217
00:12:22.045 --> 00:12:23.699
That was the last of our morphine.

218
00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:25.546
At this rate. we're gonna
burn through most of

219
00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:27.010
our supplies before the day is done.

220
00:12:27.094 --> 00:12:28.419
Patients won't survive surgeries like this.

221
00:12:28.443 --> 00:12:30.271
They're gonna die of shock.

222
00:12:30.401 --> 00:12:31.446
So what can we do?

223
00:12:31.576 --> 00:12:33.448
Alcohol is the next best sedative.

224
00:12:33.535 --> 00:12:34.928
Higher the proof. the better.

225
00:12:35.885 --> 00:12:37.495
Not a goddamn chance.

226
00:12:37.582 --> 00:12:40.542
Why don't you raid that magical
pantry you're so proud of?

227
00:12:40.629 --> 00:12:43.545
That is food. Negan. We need alcohol.

228
00:12:43.632 --> 00:12:45.218
All right. you know what?
Just to be clear.

229
00:12:45.242 --> 00:12:46.809
Dillard and I only care about

230
00:12:46.940 --> 00:12:49.464
holding on to our shit
and not giving it away.

231
00:12:49.551 --> 00:12:53.120
And while we're on the topic.
these people are clearly

232
00:12:53.207 --> 00:12:56.079
only a threat to each other
and not our shit.

233
00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:57.777
which makes this shit...

234
00:12:57.864 --> 00:12:59.024
beyond the scope of shit that

235
00:12:59.082 --> 00:13:00.692
we need to be giving a shit about.

236
00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:02.303
She's really hurting. man.

237
00:13:07.874 --> 00:13:10.615
Fine. go get the damn whiskey.

238
00:13:14.271 --> 00:13:16.752
I am gonna go have a smoke.

239
00:13:19.276 --> 00:13:22.802
Hey. I appreciate what you
and Dillard are doing.

240
00:13:22.932 --> 00:13:25.171
Alright. well. the more time
he gets to spend with people.

241
00:13:25.195 --> 00:13:28.329
the less with corpses.
is a win for both of us.

242
00:13:28.416 --> 00:13:30.113
So you're doing this for him?

243
00:13:31.593 --> 00:13:33.247
You really don't give a shit?

244
00:13:34.117 --> 00:13:35.858
Gold star. counselor.

245
00:13:35.989 --> 00:13:37.555
You cracked the case.

246
00:13:37.686 --> 00:13:39.731
You know. Maggie said
this was your idea.

247
00:13:39.862 --> 00:13:42.343
- bringing in more people.
- Idea. sure.

248
00:13:42.473 --> 00:13:45.737
Piss poor execution? Hell no.

249
00:13:45.825 --> 00:13:47.827
Look. I don't get why we patch up people

250
00:13:47.957 --> 00:13:49.959
and then let them go kill each other.

251
00:13:50.090 --> 00:13:53.963
You pick a side. you treat them.
you have their loyalty forever.

252
00:13:54.094 --> 00:13:55.835
That is the safe play.

253
00:13:57.358 --> 00:14:00.927
Well. the safest play is to kill 'em all.

254
00:14:03.799 --> 00:14:06.976
Well. The lady has a good point.

255
00:14:07.107 --> 00:14:10.327
Of course. then
who would plant the fields?

256
00:14:10.458 --> 00:14:12.025
Who would fix the sewers?

257
00:14:12.112 --> 00:14:13.896
Who would protect our homes?

258
00:14:14.549 --> 00:14:17.900
Yes. I can make a choice
that would save us today.

259
00:14:17.987 --> 00:14:19.771
But it might lead to our deaths a month.

260
00:14:19.859 --> 00:14:21.338
a year. a decade from now.

261
00:14:21.469 --> 00:14:26.039
So I am not making any decision
until I have all the facts.

262
00:14:33.742 --> 00:14:36.092
- My turn!
- Everything is fine.

263
00:14:36.223 --> 00:14:39.052
Okay. it's just
a temporary loss in voltage.

264
00:14:39.139 --> 00:14:40.739
This has happened before. We'll be okay.

265
00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:43.230
- He's in a lot of pain.
- I know.

266
00:14:43.360 --> 00:14:44.753
We're gonna get something for it.

267
00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:46.120
Did Damien breathe in any smoke?

268
00:14:46.146 --> 00:14:47.538
We all did.

269
00:14:47.625 --> 00:14:50.585
- Belleville burnt down our home.
- Are you their leader?

270
00:14:50.715 --> 00:14:52.630
Bauer said your people started the fire.

271
00:14:52.761 --> 00:14:55.111
Of course he did.
He's a liar and a monster.

272
00:14:55.242 --> 00:14:56.682
Luis! He's having trouble breathing.

273
00:15:00.725 --> 00:15:02.553
It's Ray. He's not doing so good.

274
00:15:03.293 --> 00:15:05.774
Hershel. sterilize his
neck under his Adam's apple.

275
00:15:10.518 --> 00:15:11.911
This guy's bleeding out fast.

276
00:15:11.998 --> 00:15:13.584
I'm gonna have to get him stabilized first.

277
00:15:13.608 --> 00:15:15.436
Don't you dare. Doctor's been treating

278
00:15:15.566 --> 00:15:16.848
your people for the past two hours.

279
00:15:16.872 --> 00:15:17.873
Mine are dying.

280
00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:19.831
The only person to blame is you.
Claudia.

281
00:15:19.919 --> 00:15:21.442
They're dying because of you.

282
00:15:26.186 --> 00:15:27.404
Help Damien.

283
00:15:28.231 --> 00:15:29.667
Help him now.

284
00:15:29.754 --> 00:15:32.627
Whether or not you threaten me.
I'm gonna help his people.

285
00:15:32.714 --> 00:15:34.542
And I'm gonna help yours too.

286
00:15:55.040 --> 00:15:58.087
Anyone who isn't
a hospital worker. a patient.

287
00:15:58.174 --> 00:16:00.655
or a guard needs to leave
this ER immediately.

288
00:16:02.048 --> 00:16:03.048
Let's go!

289
00:16:10.099 --> 00:16:11.598
Hershel. I'm going to treat this wound

290
00:16:11.622 --> 00:16:13.450
while you do the cricothyrotomy.

291
00:16:14.234 --> 00:16:16.366
- By myself?
- I'll guide you through it.

292
00:16:16.497 --> 00:16:18.325
Look. cutting a throat open
sounds rough.

293
00:16:18.455 --> 00:16:20.695
but it's a lot less complicated
than a compound fracture.

294
00:16:21.937 --> 00:16:23.504
We can save both their lives.

295
00:16:23.634 --> 00:16:25.071
but it means you have to do this.

296
00:16:26.463 --> 00:16:27.551
Okay.

297
00:16:28.074 --> 00:16:29.834
Ellis. I need you
to take the Belleville people

298
00:16:29.858 --> 00:16:30.902
to the apartments.

299
00:16:30.990 --> 00:16:32.097
Rose. the Newark people to the beach.

300
00:16:32.121 --> 00:16:34.254
and I want five extra guards on each.

301
00:16:34.341 --> 00:16:36.691
And tell the team downstairs
to keep the tanks full.

302
00:16:36.821 --> 00:16:38.364
The power cannot go out.
Do you understand?

303
00:16:38.388 --> 00:16:39.388
Go.

304
00:16:47.745 --> 00:16:52.402
Hey. just the two guards
I've been looking for.

305
00:16:52.489 --> 00:16:54.424
Max down in the armory
is looking for both of you.

306
00:16:54.448 --> 00:16:56.319
I will take these two.

307
00:16:57.451 --> 00:16:59.801
Door over there. Let's go.

308
00:17:07.329 --> 00:17:11.551
Ray? That's your name. right?
Stay with me. Ray.

309
00:17:11.856 --> 00:17:13.380
Can you tell me what happened?

310
00:17:13.467 --> 00:17:15.425
Newark boy did that.
He put an arrow through

311
00:17:15.512 --> 00:17:17.862
Ray's little girl and then
beat him with a crowbar.

312
00:17:19.777 --> 00:17:21.040
He's here.

313
00:17:22.301 --> 00:17:25.044
Ray. we've got to prevent
infection. stop blood loss.

314
00:17:25.174 --> 00:17:26.393
and stabilize your fracture.

315
00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:28.284
but we can't do that
until we manage your pain.

316
00:17:28.308 --> 00:17:30.179
- You feel me?
- What is it?

317
00:17:30.310 --> 00:17:33.182
I call that the Neil Armstrong.
It's mostly whiskey and Tang.

318
00:17:33.269 --> 00:17:34.618
Alright. Ready. Ray?

319
00:17:38.492 --> 00:17:39.884
Drink as much as you can.

320
00:17:46.935 --> 00:17:48.937
Hershel? Let's go.

321
00:17:49.068 --> 00:17:51.244
I need you to feel for the Adam's apple.

322
00:17:51.374 --> 00:17:53.202
Move your fingers just below it.

323
00:17:53.289 --> 00:17:54.899
That's the cricothyroid membrane.

324
00:17:55.030 --> 00:17:56.292
- You got it?
- Yeah. I got it.

325
00:17:56.379 --> 00:17:58.512
Make the incision just above that.

326
00:17:58.599 --> 00:18:01.167
Talk to me. Hershel.
Can you feel the membrane?

327
00:18:01.254 --> 00:18:02.037
- Yeah.
- Good.

328
00:18:02.168 --> 00:18:03.560
Now you got to pierce it.

329
00:18:03.691 --> 00:18:05.345
One breath. one motion.

330
00:18:09.392 --> 00:18:11.090
Okay. Got it.

331
00:18:11.220 --> 00:18:12.613
Now slide the tube in.

332
00:18:18.314 --> 00:18:20.447
Doctor. we need you over here.

333
00:18:20.534 --> 00:18:21.883
I'll be over there soon.

334
00:18:47.474 --> 00:18:48.474
Ray.

335
00:18:49.737 --> 00:18:51.260
Ray?

336
00:18:51.913 --> 00:18:53.436
Is he all right?

337
00:18:53.523 --> 00:18:55.656
He passed out. Pulse is good.

338
00:18:56.700 --> 00:18:58.267
I think Ray's good.

339
00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:00.269
We're good.

340
00:19:08.059 --> 00:19:09.191
Can you check on bed eight?

341
00:19:09.322 --> 00:19:11.193
I've got three more surgeries to prep for.

342
00:19:11.324 --> 00:19:12.325
Yeah.

343
00:19:27.035 --> 00:19:28.558
She could have killed my brother.

344
00:19:28.645 --> 00:19:31.344
- Our only doctor.
- But we didn't let that happen.

345
00:19:31.431 --> 00:19:33.955
Belleville outnumbers us.
So does Newark.

346
00:19:34.042 --> 00:19:35.522
What if... What if we heal them

347
00:19:35.652 --> 00:19:37.219
only for one of them to take over?

348
00:19:37.306 --> 00:19:38.655
Completely wipe us out?

349
00:19:38.742 --> 00:19:40.527
I know that I have to make a choice here.

350
00:19:40.657 --> 00:19:43.138
but what if there is no right choice?

351
00:19:43.269 --> 00:19:45.116
Anybody who tells you
that the solution's simple

352
00:19:45.140 --> 00:19:47.273
is answering the wrong question.

353
00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:50.406
Picking one side.
killing the other. that's easy.

354
00:19:51.059 --> 00:19:54.976
Building a safe community is
the hardest thing in the world.

355
00:19:59.023 --> 00:20:01.461
I don't know if there's a right choice.

356
00:20:02.462 --> 00:20:05.856
But if there is. you're gonna make it.

357
00:20:09.556 --> 00:20:12.385
This is what we asked for
when we turned on that light.

358
00:20:14.691 --> 00:20:15.910
Do you regret doing it?

359
00:20:17.477 --> 00:20:18.477
No.

360
00:20:19.783 --> 00:20:21.089
Do you?

361
00:20:25.485 --> 00:20:26.747
No.

362
00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:31.162
I should check on the new
arrivals in the apartment.

363
00:20:31.186 --> 00:20:32.746
Hopefully I can get some answers there.

364
00:20:42.719 --> 00:20:44.373
Hey. you okay?

365
00:21:01.521 --> 00:21:02.913
- Leonard!
- Yeah?

366
00:21:03.566 --> 00:21:04.654
We're going on lockdown.

367
00:21:04.785 --> 00:21:06.482
I want guards in the pantry
and the armory.

368
00:21:06.569 --> 00:21:08.571
With everything happening.
we can't be too careful.

369
00:21:08.702 --> 00:21:09.746
You got it.

370
00:21:09.833 --> 00:21:10.660
Hey. guys! We're going on lockdown!

371
00:21:10.791 --> 00:21:12.009
Where the hell is Negan?

372
00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:13.460
I'm gonna need you in the armory.

373
00:21:18.320 --> 00:21:20.366
Shoulda faced
the truth and just moved on.

374
00:21:20.453 --> 00:21:21.454
Moved on how?

375
00:21:21.541 --> 00:21:23.061
After you destroyed everything we had?

376
00:21:25.632 --> 00:21:27.111
Two groups of people.

377
00:21:28.112 --> 00:21:29.940
But only one can stay.

378
00:21:30.941 --> 00:21:33.074
However will we decide?

379
00:21:37.383 --> 00:21:40.124
See. I used to know this...

380
00:21:40.255 --> 00:21:42.779
Well. we'll call him an asshole.

381
00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:46.087
And he would ask people
three questions.

382
00:21:46.174 --> 00:21:47.654
and that would decide whether or not

383
00:21:47.784 --> 00:21:50.134
they would stay as part
of the community.

384
00:21:50.831 --> 00:21:54.661
But see. I am not in the mood
to be asking any questions.

385
00:21:56.097 --> 00:21:57.794
So we're gonna play a game.

386
00:21:59.056 --> 00:22:02.016
We are gonna play Piñata.

387
00:22:02.146 --> 00:22:06.020
And you two are stuffed full of

388
00:22:06.150 --> 00:22:08.457
poo-poo-flavored candy.

389
00:22:09.632 --> 00:22:10.851
Dillard!

390
00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:13.984
See. Dillard. occasionally

391
00:22:14.115 --> 00:22:16.378
you have to crack a couple eggs.

392
00:22:16.465 --> 00:22:17.790
Otherwise. you're left cleaning up

393
00:22:17.814 --> 00:22:20.426
a big-ol' eggy mess.

394
00:22:24.255 --> 00:22:29.130
I am tired of the he said/she said bullshit.

395
00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:32.829
So we're gonna let Dizzy Dillard
here take some swings

396
00:22:32.960 --> 00:22:34.309
until one of you volunteer

397
00:22:34.396 --> 00:22:36.964
to take your people out of Manhattan.

398
00:22:38.008 --> 00:22:39.662
Dillard?

399
00:22:59.595 --> 00:23:01.075
Shh...

400
00:23:02.946 --> 00:23:06.428
Oopsie-daisy.

401
00:23:08.082 --> 00:23:10.432
Somebody forgot to pay the power bill!

402
00:23:10.519 --> 00:23:12.869
You know how we make electricity?

403
00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:14.523
Bodies.

404
00:23:14.610 --> 00:23:17.004
That's right. We live off the dead.

405
00:23:17.091 --> 00:23:20.094
So unless one of you pipes up.

406
00:23:20.224 --> 00:23:23.663
we will gladly kill all of your people.

407
00:23:27.318 --> 00:23:28.755
Seriously?

408
00:23:29.886 --> 00:23:32.628
You would rather have your kids

409
00:23:32.715 --> 00:23:35.762
power up my Xbox...

410
00:23:37.241 --> 00:23:40.375
than squash this little beef you have?

411
00:23:48.514 --> 00:23:50.777
Alright. Got that.

412
00:23:57.087 --> 00:23:58.306
Hey.

413
00:23:59.786 --> 00:24:01.527
Hey. I'm comin'.

414
00:24:04.878 --> 00:24:06.140
Yeah. I feel this one.

415
00:24:17.456 --> 00:24:18.326
Did you?

416
00:24:18.413 --> 00:24:19.762
Come on.

417
00:24:19.849 --> 00:24:21.889
We just had a little bit of
a heart-to-heart is all.

418
00:24:22.286 --> 00:24:24.071
Look. I don't know who started it.

419
00:24:24.158 --> 00:24:26.987
but neither asshole is innocent.

420
00:24:27.074 --> 00:24:28.510
The war is not gonna end.

421
00:24:28.641 --> 00:24:30.207
which means all we got to do is...

422
00:24:31.470 --> 00:24:33.646
Wow. Still?

423
00:24:33.733 --> 00:24:35.517
- For reals with this?
- Christ.

424
00:24:35.648 --> 00:24:37.388
How many guards does it take
to load a tank?

425
00:24:37.476 --> 00:24:38.476
More.

426
00:24:41.480 --> 00:24:43.040
What the hell
are they doing down there?

427
00:24:44.221 --> 00:24:46.572
You are so gonna owe us.

428
00:24:48.661 --> 00:24:52.534
No! No. wake up!

429
00:24:52.621 --> 00:24:55.798
Please. stay!

430
00:24:59.802 --> 00:25:01.587
Hershel. no!

431
00:25:05.852 --> 00:25:07.201
I have to try.

432
00:25:40.713 --> 00:25:42.279
All four ventilators just went down.

433
00:25:42.366 --> 00:25:43.779
If we don't Ambu bag. they're
brain dead in five minutes.

434
00:25:43.803 --> 00:25:46.327
Here. bag Damien. Can you do bed six?

435
00:25:46.414 --> 00:25:48.111
- Yep.
- Ever done this before?

436
00:25:48.198 --> 00:25:49.198
Once.

437
00:25:49.243 --> 00:25:50.636
Connect it to the breathing tube.

438
00:25:50.723 --> 00:25:52.643
- Squeeze every six seconds.
- Every six seconds.

439
00:26:22.972 --> 00:26:24.278
Mom. duck!

440
00:26:29.413 --> 00:26:30.676
Bone saw. wall cabinet.

441
00:26:40.424 --> 00:26:41.817
Here.

442
00:26:41.904 --> 00:26:43.384
Please. Please.

443
00:26:43.471 --> 00:26:45.691
Do you have anything
to give me for the pain?

444
00:26:48.084 --> 00:26:49.738
It's the best I've got.

445
00:27:07.626 --> 00:27:09.323
By the time I get down here...

446
00:27:11.238 --> 00:27:12.631
They turned.

447
00:27:12.761 --> 00:27:14.001
Must have got bit by a patient.

448
00:27:16.417 --> 00:27:19.463
Alright. come on.
Dillweed. let's keep movin'.

449
00:27:26.122 --> 00:27:27.471
Dillard.

450
00:27:33.782 --> 00:27:36.002
Aah! Get off me!

451
00:27:36.132 --> 00:27:38.004
Aah!

452
00:27:39.527 --> 00:27:41.921
- Help me! Help me!
- Stay under there!

453
00:28:11.951 --> 00:28:13.169
Hey. man.

454
00:28:13.909 --> 00:28:17.217
Shit!

455
00:28:22.831 --> 00:28:24.703
We should've stayed at the bar.

456
00:28:26.748 --> 00:28:28.588
It's good to get out on the town
with you. man.

457
00:28:32.362 --> 00:28:33.712
We need to bag bed three soon.

458
00:28:33.842 --> 00:28:35.844
Hey. I know you're at war with these two.

459
00:28:35.931 --> 00:28:38.847
If they die. we all die. Can't you help?

460
00:28:49.031 --> 00:28:50.119
- Luis?!
- I got it!

461
00:28:50.206 --> 00:28:51.773
Keep bagging!

462
00:29:11.575 --> 00:29:13.229
Help me!

463
00:29:13.316 --> 00:29:16.015
Help me! Help me!

464
00:29:18.582 --> 00:29:19.845
Help me!

465
00:29:25.894 --> 00:29:29.071
- Hershel. did you hear that?
- Hear what?

466
00:29:32.553 --> 00:29:33.859
One.

467
00:29:35.556 --> 00:29:36.949
Two.

468
00:29:39.429 --> 00:29:40.561
Three.

469
00:29:45.958 --> 00:29:47.263
Four.

470
00:29:49.265 --> 00:29:50.745
Five.

471
00:29:52.051 --> 00:29:53.139
Six.

472
00:30:42.188 --> 00:30:44.190
Hey. What's up. Doc?

473
00:30:48.847 --> 00:30:50.457
How am I supposed to tell his family

474
00:30:50.544 --> 00:30:52.024
he died from a broken arm?

475
00:30:53.416 --> 00:30:54.591
We do it together.

476
00:30:55.418 --> 00:30:58.073
We tell them it could have been
an embolism from the fracture

477
00:30:58.160 --> 00:30:59.901
or something completely unrelated.

478
00:30:59.988 --> 00:31:01.642
a heart attack or aneurysm.

479
00:31:01.990 --> 00:31:03.470
Because that's all we know.

480
00:31:04.819 --> 00:31:05.951
Hey.

481
00:31:07.256 --> 00:31:08.388
You lost a patient.

482
00:31:09.389 --> 00:31:10.389
It hurts.

483
00:31:11.086 --> 00:31:12.740
It'll always hurt.

484
00:31:15.134 --> 00:31:16.613
Look at the people you saved.

485
00:31:25.666 --> 00:31:30.801
Listen. I know this medical
school throws you right in.

486
00:31:30.889 --> 00:31:34.370
and the student social life. well. sucks.

487
00:31:35.154 --> 00:31:36.895
But I will tell you. you're gonna earn

488
00:31:37.025 --> 00:31:38.940
a pretty kick-ass handwritten

489
00:31:39.027 --> 00:31:41.073
certificate of doctor hood from me.

490
00:31:42.378 --> 00:31:43.423
Framed.

491
00:31:50.560 --> 00:31:52.998
Bauer and Claudia. they are locked

492
00:31:53.085 --> 00:31:57.741
into this prick-measuring
contest of epic-ass proportions.

493
00:31:57.828 --> 00:31:59.178
The fact of the matter is.

494
00:31:59.265 --> 00:32:01.310
and I do know you love your facts.

495
00:32:01.441 --> 00:32:04.661
you can choose a group to stay
and send the other one off.

496
00:32:04.748 --> 00:32:06.881
but it's just a matter
of time before the next attack.

497
00:32:06.968 --> 00:32:10.276
So you let them finish their little war.

498
00:32:10.929 --> 00:32:14.410
Whichever group survives. stays.

499
00:32:15.107 --> 00:32:16.108
You're right.

500
00:32:17.196 --> 00:32:19.285
This war does have to end.

501
00:32:19.415 --> 00:32:21.809
As long as these groups are
fighting each other.

502
00:32:21.940 --> 00:32:23.376
Manhattan is at risk.

503
00:32:23.463 --> 00:32:26.640
And yes. letting them battle to the death.

504
00:32:26.727 --> 00:32:28.381
that is a solution.

505
00:32:28.468 --> 00:32:32.254
But it can't be the only one.

506
00:32:33.516 --> 00:32:35.823
We three. we were enemies
when we first met.

507
00:32:35.954 --> 00:32:37.303
Until the baby gave us

508
00:32:37.433 --> 00:32:39.566
something to work for together.

509
00:32:39.653 --> 00:32:41.611
We gotta give 'em something to fight for.

510
00:32:46.616 --> 00:32:48.314
Revenge is a cage.

511
00:32:48.749 --> 00:32:53.101
The only escape comes from
putting our emotions aside.

512
00:32:56.713 --> 00:32:58.933
These fields are enormous.

513
00:32:59.586 --> 00:33:02.371
It will take each
and every one of your hands

514
00:33:02.458 --> 00:33:03.720
to bring it to life.

515
00:33:04.547 --> 00:33:08.725
Now. you can use these scythes
to turn on each other.

516
00:33:08.812 --> 00:33:12.903
or you could use these scythes

517
00:33:12.991 --> 00:33:15.994
to turn this parkland into farmland.

518
00:33:17.647 --> 00:33:20.215
Here. survival is not enough.

519
00:33:20.824 --> 00:33:25.699
Here. together. we live.

520
00:34:48.824 --> 00:34:51.741
Well. maybe she does got it.

521
00:35:02.317 --> 00:35:04.363
I don't know what happened
across the river.

522
00:35:04.972 --> 00:35:06.887
But your people are putting
it behind them.

523
00:35:08.584 --> 00:35:09.933
Can you?

524
00:35:42.140 --> 00:35:43.402
Hey.

525
00:35:45.055 --> 00:35:46.840
Hershel was a star today.

526
00:35:48.972 --> 00:35:50.104
You're a good teacher.

527
00:35:51.540 --> 00:35:52.628
Thank you.

528
00:35:53.586 --> 00:35:55.153
There you go. Steady.

529
00:35:56.545 --> 00:35:59.287
- How many more are coming in?
- That's it.

530
00:35:59.418 --> 00:36:01.420
Bauer and Claudia couldn't move past.

531
00:36:01.507 --> 00:36:05.946
But 146 out of 148 chose hope.

532
00:36:11.081 --> 00:36:12.605
There's good people here.

533
00:36:13.519 --> 00:36:15.347
And we saved a few of them today.

534
00:36:15.434 --> 00:36:18.045
No. You did.

535
00:36:19.873 --> 00:36:21.527
They're alive because you lit that light.

536
00:36:22.092 --> 00:36:23.137
You took a chance.

537
00:36:23.833 --> 00:36:25.183
You both did.

538
00:36:27.881 --> 00:36:29.187
You were right to.

539
00:36:31.537 --> 00:36:34.714
I've just been thinking about Ramon.

540
00:36:36.194 --> 00:36:37.195
Chucho.

541
00:36:38.674 --> 00:36:39.806
Marisol.

542
00:36:43.201 --> 00:36:45.812
The idea of losing someone else is just...

543
00:36:46.682 --> 00:36:47.770
Hey.

544
00:36:47.857 --> 00:36:49.207
Luisito.

545
00:36:52.384 --> 00:36:53.385
I know.

546
00:36:54.386 --> 00:36:56.083
I know.

547
00:36:56.214 --> 00:36:57.389
It's okay.

548
00:36:59.521 --> 00:37:00.566
Yeah.

549
00:37:02.959 --> 00:37:05.223
Yeah. It's gonna be.

550
00:37:12.099 --> 00:37:14.144
I'm looking forward to
looking forward again.

551
00:37:28.550 --> 00:37:30.509
Seeing you at the hospital today.

552
00:37:30.596 --> 00:37:33.251
you made me so proud.

553
00:37:34.774 --> 00:37:36.254
You're working so hard.

554
00:37:38.473 --> 00:37:39.473
I like it.

555
00:37:39.518 --> 00:37:41.433
Do you? I can tell.

556
00:37:45.741 --> 00:37:47.439
My daddy was a good man.

557
00:37:50.398 --> 00:37:53.619
And I see so much of
his goodness in you.

558
00:37:56.926 --> 00:38:00.452
This was his and his father's before him.

559
00:38:00.539 --> 00:38:02.280
And now it belongs to you.

560
00:38:06.936 --> 00:38:08.634
Thank you.

561
00:38:22.691 --> 00:38:25.955
Everything that you did today.
you're the best leader

562
00:38:26.086 --> 00:38:27.166
that this place could have.

563
00:38:27.217 --> 00:38:29.307
Youkept us all safe.

564
00:38:37.576 --> 00:38:39.296
We're building the place
that we dreamed of.

565
00:38:40.230 --> 00:38:42.972
It's... actually happening.

566
00:38:43.364 --> 00:38:46.846
Which just makes it
so much scarier. right?

567
00:38:51.633 --> 00:38:53.679
I've been in so many places
that didn't make it.

568
00:38:55.594 --> 00:38:57.160
And this one is different.

569
00:38:59.467 --> 00:39:00.686
If we can't make it work

570
00:39:00.773 --> 00:39:02.446
with everything
that we've got going for us.

571
00:39:02.470 --> 00:39:04.037
I don't think that we ever will.

572
00:39:04.820 --> 00:39:05.865
I know.

573
00:39:06.779 --> 00:39:09.956
But I also know that
we made it through today.

574
00:39:11.305 --> 00:39:12.959
Yes. we did.

575
00:39:15.396 --> 00:39:17.529
Tomorrow's going to look so different.

576
00:39:18.834 --> 00:39:20.096
With this many more people.

577
00:39:20.227 --> 00:39:22.055
there's just so much more to consider.

578
00:39:22.142 --> 00:39:24.884
The hospital is almost out
of meds and methane.

579
00:39:26.581 --> 00:39:28.453
We're gonna have
to schedule power outages.

580
00:39:28.540 --> 00:39:30.237
And until we clear more blocks.

581
00:39:30.324 --> 00:39:34.110
set up housing for everyone.
we're gonna need

582
00:39:34.197 --> 00:39:36.548
something solid between us
and the walkers.

583
00:39:37.984 --> 00:39:39.681
That's for tomorrow.

584
00:39:40.900 --> 00:39:43.381
Let's take tonight to appreciate today.

585
00:39:47.385 --> 00:39:48.647
Can I be honest with you?

586
00:39:49.474 --> 00:39:51.258
I cannot stand champagne.

587
00:39:51.389 --> 00:39:52.829
It tastes like cat piss. doesn't it?

588
00:39:52.912 --> 00:39:54.087
It really does.

589
00:39:54.392 --> 00:39:56.916
Yes!

590
00:39:58.004 --> 00:39:59.397
Much better.

591
00:40:00.659 --> 00:40:01.747
Salud.

592
00:40:09.972 --> 00:40:11.931
Holy meth lab. Crackman!
What is happening?

593
00:40:12.061 --> 00:40:13.061
Ha ha!

594
00:40:13.106 --> 00:40:15.543
Look. we may have lost the whiskey.

595
00:40:15.630 --> 00:40:18.633
but we are never gonna run out of booze.

596
00:40:18.938 --> 00:40:22.028
Just happened one
of those Belleville bastards

597
00:40:22.115 --> 00:40:24.596
is also a bathtub gin wizard.

598
00:40:24.726 --> 00:40:27.337
I like the sound of that.
What is happening in my bar?

599
00:40:27.425 --> 00:40:29.514
- Well. I'm glad you asked.
- Okay.

600
00:40:31.429 --> 00:40:33.648
- Follow me.
- With pleasure. brother.

601
00:40:39.915 --> 00:40:41.395
Now don't get used to it.

602
00:40:41.482 --> 00:40:43.266
I'm just giving the Xbox the night off.

603
00:40:43.353 --> 00:40:45.007
I did say you were gonna get laid. right?

604
00:40:45.138 --> 00:40:47.532
And you were on a bit of a roll today.

605
00:40:48.097 --> 00:40:50.099
So pick a girl. Any girl.

606
00:40:50.839 --> 00:40:52.275
Or boy. Whatever...

607
00:40:52.362 --> 00:40:54.321
Whatever floats your freaky boat.

608
00:40:56.715 --> 00:40:59.108
I think I smell... methaney. actually.

609
00:40:59.195 --> 00:41:00.608
I should probably change
my clothes. bro.

610
00:41:00.632 --> 00:41:02.808
- I'll be right back. Okay.
- Alright.

611
00:41:02.938 --> 00:41:04.287
Okay.

612
00:41:16.474 --> 00:41:18.998
He's turning you against us.

613
00:41:19.085 --> 00:41:20.347
Against me.

614
00:41:20.478 --> 00:41:22.175
Hey. stop it.

615
00:41:22.305 --> 00:41:23.872
That man is no good.

616
00:41:23.959 --> 00:41:25.047
I swear if I ever...

617
00:41:25.178 --> 00:41:26.701
Hey. stop.

618
00:41:26.832 --> 00:41:29.225
I'm sorry. I get so jealous.

619
00:41:30.879 --> 00:41:32.185
Stay with me tonight.

620
00:41:32.315 --> 00:41:34.404
I said I can't. okay?

621
00:41:34.535 --> 00:41:35.971
- Hey!
- Please.

622
00:41:36.058 --> 00:41:38.496
- I miss you.
- No!

623
00:41:40.628 --> 00:41:44.066
I love you.

624
00:41:51.944 --> 00:41:53.032
Are you the traitor?

625
00:41:53.119 --> 00:41:54.163
Can I help you?

626
00:41:54.294 --> 00:41:55.374
We've come to make a deal.

627
00:41:57.297 --> 00:41:59.342
This woman can get
her hands on anything.

628
00:41:59.429 --> 00:42:01.127
You're sending our only doctor away?

629
00:42:01.214 --> 00:42:02.868
I need you to make sure he's safe.

630
00:42:04.913 --> 00:42:07.133
If I live here.
I have to live under your rules?

631
00:42:07.263 --> 00:42:08.983
You follow the same rules
as everyone else.

632
00:42:10.832 --> 00:42:13.226
If this is real. it could be dangerous.

633
00:42:14.270 --> 00:42:16.621
This is the start of
something better for everyone.

634
00:42:21.713 --> 00:42:23.149
Hi. everyone. I'm Aimee Garcia.

635
00:42:23.236 --> 00:42:25.151
I play Renata on "Dead City"
season three.

636
00:42:25.238 --> 00:42:26.631
Welcome. Muah!

637
00:42:31.940 --> 00:42:33.420
Renata is the leader of her family.

638
00:42:33.507 --> 00:42:35.422
When her father passed away.

639
00:42:35.509 --> 00:42:37.424
she really had to step up
and take the reins.

640
00:42:37.555 --> 00:42:40.819
And she also becomes
the leader of her community.

641
00:42:40.906 --> 00:42:42.971
Everything The Croat had said
about this place is true.

642
00:42:42.995 --> 00:42:44.997
It is a fortress.

643
00:42:45.127 --> 00:42:49.044
The only thing
that we are missing is someone

644
00:42:49.131 --> 00:42:50.369
who knows how to keep things safe.

645
00:42:50.393 --> 00:42:52.657
Maggie.

646
00:42:52.744 --> 00:42:53.527
I've always loved that
character. and I always thought.

647
00:42:53.658 --> 00:42:55.181
"we could be friends."

648
00:42:55.311 --> 00:42:57.444
Now we get to be besties.

649
00:42:57.575 --> 00:43:00.795
Let's take tonight to appreciate today.

650
00:43:00.882 --> 00:43:01.927
I had said to Seth.

651
00:43:02.057 --> 00:43:03.885
"Please write a BFF for Maggie

652
00:43:03.972 --> 00:43:05.800
because she's just been up against it.

653
00:43:05.887 --> 00:43:07.767
and it's like she's
been trying to carve her way

654
00:43:07.846 --> 00:43:09.238
through this ocean of enemies

655
00:43:09.325 --> 00:43:12.894
"it has felt like for a few years."

656
00:43:13.025 --> 00:43:14.113
You haven't had a gal pal.

657
00:43:14.200 --> 00:43:15.767
- Right?
- Yeah.

658
00:43:15.897 --> 00:43:17.856
They both are big-hearted warriors.

659
00:43:17.943 --> 00:43:20.183
I think there's a complete
mutual respect for each other.

660
00:43:20.293 --> 00:43:24.602
They both have a natural
magnetic leadership quality.

661
00:43:24.732 --> 00:43:27.126
And I think Renata brings out.

662
00:43:27.256 --> 00:43:29.607
hopefully a light in Maggie. too.

663
00:43:29.694 --> 00:43:31.434
I cannot stand champagne.

664
00:43:31.521 --> 00:43:32.890
It tastes like cat piss. doesn't it?

665
00:43:32.914 --> 00:43:35.047
It really does.

666
00:43:35.177 --> 00:43:38.877
I just feel like you root for this friendship.

667
00:43:38.964 --> 00:43:42.924
Building a safe community is
the hardest thing in the world.

668
00:43:43.055 --> 00:43:45.255
This is what we asked for
when we turned on that light.

669
00:43:45.318 --> 00:43:47.581
What Renata brings to the storyline

670
00:43:47.712 --> 00:43:50.628
is this level
of heart and family and warmth

671
00:43:50.715 --> 00:43:54.501
that has been missing
for our characters for so long.

672
00:43:54.632 --> 00:43:56.677
Renata is charismatic.
she's levelheaded.

673
00:43:56.808 --> 00:43:58.070
She's a total badass.

674
00:43:58.157 --> 00:44:00.550
She actually has this weapon.

675
00:44:00.638 --> 00:44:06.165
which I have personally named
Bonita because it is a bone saw.

676
00:44:06.252 --> 00:44:08.733
This is my first time
with Renata's weapon

677
00:44:08.820 --> 00:44:09.821
and I'm being sensei'd.

678
00:44:09.908 --> 00:44:11.692
Go on.

679
00:44:11.779 --> 00:44:13.278
I thought that name
would be very appropriate.

680
00:44:13.302 --> 00:44:15.783
Bonita means "pretty" in Spanish.

681
00:44:15.914 --> 00:44:17.785
Lauren gave me a great tip

682
00:44:17.916 --> 00:44:20.353
because she said. "You should
grunt when you kill a walker."

683
00:44:22.355 --> 00:44:24.139
And she says it does multiple things.

684
00:44:24.226 --> 00:44:27.665
It warns the stunt person
that you're coming

685
00:44:27.752 --> 00:44:30.363
and it also makes you feel less awkward.

686
00:44:32.234 --> 00:44:34.410
Tips from the pro.

687
00:44:34.497 --> 00:44:37.544
I'm literally putting
my life in Lauren's hands.

688
00:44:37.675 --> 00:44:40.112
Shit!

689
00:44:40.242 --> 00:44:42.375
Wow. The head fell
right towards the camera.

690
00:44:42.462 --> 00:44:44.507
Lauren is amazing.

691
00:44:44.594 --> 00:44:47.380
She is such a fearless leader in real life.

692
00:44:47.510 --> 00:44:49.774
She's a great quarterback of this team.

693
00:44:49.904 --> 00:44:51.819
I love her and I hope
to be friends with her

694
00:44:51.950 --> 00:44:52.950
for a very long time.
